                "while keeping host escape hatches controlled by posture.\n"
                "\n"
                "Why it exists:\n"
                "- Normal Sandworm sandboxes intentionally **mask** `/workspace/.sandworm` so tools and models cannot\n"
                "  accidentally read the control plane.\n"
                "- But when you are developing Sandworm itself, Sandworm needs its control plane to be present so it can\n"
                "  run `build singlefile`, run the test facility, and emit run artifacts.\n"
                "\n"
                "So the cockpit is an explicit dev-only lane that:\n"
                "- Runs a sandbox (default: **bwrap**; optional: **kvm**) to work on the repo from inside Sandworm.\n"
                "- In bwrap, exposes the full control plane inside the sandbox at `/workspace/.sandworm`.\n"
                "- In KVM, posture remains safe-only.\n"
                "- Keeps posture semantics: `safe|dev` deny host actions; `unsafe|take-the-wheel` enable host gateway and/or `/host` per posture contract.\n"
                "\n"
                "Start the cockpit:\n"
                "```bash\n"
                "# Default: posture=safe.\n"
                "sandworm dev cockpit\n"
                "\n"
                "# KVM cockpit lane: safe-only guest workflow.\n"
                "sandworm dev cockpit --backend kvm\n"
                "\n"
                "# With explicit host escape posture (dangerous).\n"
                "sandworm dev cockpit --posture unsafe\n"
                "sandworm dev cockpit --posture take-the-wheel\n"
                "\n"
                "Note: `--backend kvm` currently supports `--posture safe` only.\n"
                "\n"
                "# Non-interactive (run a command and exit).\n"
                "sandworm dev cockpit -- sh -lc 'sandworm doctor --json'\n"
                "\n"
                "# Networking debug (inside the cockpit):\n"
